    "description": "Grade II* Listed Modernist building, famously described by Walter Gropius as \"an oasis of glass in a desert of brick\". Originally built to house 'The Peckham Experiment' an innovative health centre in the 1930s. It was converted to private dwellings in 2000, retaining the indoor pool. \r\n\r\nJoin members of our new Community Interest Company set up to mark the centenary and share this unique story.",
